# shellcheck shell=bash
# =============================================================================
#  site.jean-zay.sh.example — the site configuration the published numbers used
# =============================================================================
#
#  This is the machine-specific half of scripts/slurm/env.sh, as it was on
#  Jean-Zay (IDRIS), the cluster that produced every number in Table 1. It is
#  shipped as an EXAMPLE for two reasons:
#
#    * provenance — these are the exact roots, module set and proxy the campaign
#      ran against, and they document what "the same environment" means;
#    * portability — none of them exist anywhere else, so no one should inherit
#      them by default. env.sh's own defaults are derived from $SCRATCH / $WORK /
#      $HOME and name no machine, project or user.
#
#  To use it (on Jean-Zay, or as a template elsewhere):
#
#      cd scripts/slurm
#      cp site.jean-zay.sh.example site.local.sh
#      $EDITOR site.local.sh                 # replace the paths with your own
#
#  env.sh sources site.local.sh (from <repo>/ or from scripts/slurm/) BEFORE it
#  applies any default, so everything set here wins. site.local.sh is gitignored;
#  this .example file is committed. The older name local_paths.sh is still read
#  too, for checkouts that already have one.
#
#  Anything you would rather not keep in a file can equally be exported in the
#  shell before `sbatch` — SLURM copies the submitting environment into the job.
#
#  Note that the #SBATCH directives (account, partition, QoS, constraint,
#  walltime) live inside each .slurm file and are NOT set from here; SLURM parses
#  them before any shell runs. See the header of env.sh for what each one means
#  and what to change off-site.
# =============================================================================

# A label for the env.sh banner, so a log makes clear which site file was active.
NN_L1_SBI_SITE="Jean-Zay (IDRIS)"

# ---- writable data root ------------------------------------------------------
# $SCRATCH on Jean-Zay: high-throughput Lustre, purged after 30 days idle. This is
# also what env.sh's portable default resolves to when $SCRATCH is set, so the
# line is here for explicitness rather than necessity.
# NN_L1_SBI_DATA="$SCRATCH/nn_l1_sbi"

# ---- bulk inputs -------------------------------------------------------------
# The cross TFDS (~290 GB) holding
# nbody_cosmogrid_dataset_tomo_cross/grid_10deg_80px_nonoverlap180 — the training
# set. It is not rebuilt by any job in this tree.
NN_L1_SBI_TFDS="/lustre/fsn1/projects/rech/prk/ulx34io/tensorflow_datasets"

# CosmoGridV1, as an IDRIS-wide shared read-only dataset (not a personal copy).
# Only the fiducial observation cache and the sigma tables read it.
NN_L1_SBI_COSMOGRID="/lustre/fsmisc/dataset/CosmoGridV1"

# The frozen BNT per-(channel,scale) noise-sigma table: the SNR denominator of the
# flat-local l1 binning in the BNT frame. This is the original file the campaign
# read, produced by the earlier flatsky-cross work, and the no-BNT twin that
# setup/freeze_sigma.slurm rebuilds is cross-checked field by field against it.
NN_L1_SBI_SIGMA_BNT="/lustre/fsn1/projects/rech/prk/ulx34io/cnn_sbi/scripts/sbi/results/exploratory/flatsky_cross_2026_06/flatsky_cross_noise_sigma_bnt.npz"

# ---- python environment ------------------------------------------------------
# The pinned env ("jaxili"), built by setup/build_env.slurm from
# inputs/env_freeze.txt + inputs/constraints.txt. On $WORK, not $SCRATCH: conda
# environments are hundreds of thousands of small files and $WORK has the inode
# headroom.
NN_L1_SBI_ENV="/lustre/fswork/projects/rech/nzu/ulx34io/envs/jaxili"
# NN_L1_SBI_PYTHON defaults to $NN_L1_SBI_ENV/bin/python; set it explicitly to use
# an interpreter that is not inside NN_L1_SBI_ENV.
# NN_L1_SBI_PYTHON="$NN_L1_SBI_ENV/bin/python"

# ---- modules -----------------------------------------------------------------
# IDRIS module names, per NN_L1_SBI_ARCH (each job sets it before sourcing env.sh).
# arch/a100 switches the module tree to the A100 partition (gpu_p5) — it is
# required there and does not exist elsewhere. env.sh's portable default for all
# three is ":" (load nothing).
NN_L1_SBI_MODULES_GPU="module purge; module load arch/a100; module load python/3.11.5"
NN_L1_SBI_MODULES_CPU="module purge; module load python/3.11.5"
NN_L1_SBI_MODULES_BUILD="module purge; module load miniforge"

# ---- outbound network --------------------------------------------------------
# IDRIS compute nodes have no internet; the prepost partition reaches PyPI only
# through this proxy. Used by setup/build_env.slurm alone (setup/install_env.slurm
# is the offline route). Leave empty on a site with direct access.
NN_L1_SBI_HTTP_PROXY="http://prodprox.idris.fr:3128"

# ---- optional ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The five one-off patch-centre drivers are not shipped with the package; point
# this at the directory holding them if you have them (see setup/find_centers.slurm).
# NN_L1_SBI_CENTERS_SRC="/path/to/centers/drivers"
#
# Offline wheelhouse for setup/install_env.slurm (~12 GB, disposable).
# NN_L1_SBI_WHEELHOUSE="$NN_L1_SBI_DATA/wheelhouse"
